WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:07.330
My goodness, today might be a historic day,
because Google DeepMind’s ChatGPT competitor,

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.840
Gemini is here.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:15.730
We were wondering what kind of secret AI does
google have up its sleeve, and today, you

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.279
will know all about it.

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:24.250
I am so excited, and I was also surprised
by this appearing as I was catching up on

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:31.480
some music albums to listen to, and found
a new favorite song with the same name, what

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.730
are the chances!

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.530
So, what can the Gemini AI do?

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.930
Boy, did they come out with guns blazing.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.539
Thus, Gemini has a lot to offer.

00:00:42.539 --> 00:00:49.520
According to the marketing materials, it is
absolutely insane, and fortunately, look!

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:50.520
Yes!

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.520
Haha!

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.719
We also have a paper to have a look at together.

00:00:54.719 --> 00:01:01.109
This is a multimodal AI, it can have a look
at your math homework, with handwritten notes,

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:05.710
no need to type in anything, just a photo,
and look!

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:10.780
It already found a silly little mistake in
this physics derivation.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.830
It explains what went wrong and how to do
it right beautifully.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:21.829
It can even give you new practice problems
and analyze your answers to that.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:22.979
A personal teacher.

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:24.660
That is amazing.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:28.770
But note that ChatGPT can do this too.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:34.210
We’ll see in a moment if it can do things
that ChatGPT cannot.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.549
And we are not done yet.

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:37.740
Not even close.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.270
In fact, we are just warming up.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:44.790
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.430
Now, have a look at this paper.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:53.060
This is a meta analysis on different genetic
variants of particular diseases.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:58.329
This means a research paper, written by hand
by looking up tens of thousands and thousands

00:01:58.329 --> 00:02:04.119
of papers, finding the handful of papers out
of those that have relevant information to

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:10.460
a given topic, aggregate and compare their
findings, and draw a conclusion.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.280
That is a herculean task.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:19.870
And now, hold on to your papers Fellow Scholars,
because Gemini can do this automatically.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:24.550
It can evaluate papers rapidly, and see how
relevant they are.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:30.760
Now, little AI, read the paper and extract
the relevant data from it.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.760
Look!

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.510
No hallucinations allowed, because we are
seeing where it got all this data from.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:43.930
According to DeepMind, it read through hundreds
of thousands of papers in just one lunch break.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:49.710
I have to say they have incredibly productive
lunch breaks over there at DeepMind.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.710
Bravo!

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:56.870
Now it can also update the studies and the
fact that this is a multimodal AI, it means

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:02.240
that it can deal with code, audio, images,
video, you name it.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.500
Not just text.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.500
Fantastic.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:13.730
But wait a second, if it can do all of that,
is it possible that it can even write a paper?

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:14.849
Interesting question.

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:20.660
Well, little AI, update the graphs with the
new information.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.660
Wow!

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:27.930
So far, we needed this kind of herculean effort
to summarize this genetic research data up

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:34.370
to 2019, and now, we have all this data up
to 2023.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.599
And all this in just one lunch break.

00:03:37.599 --> 00:03:38.730
Automatically.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.659
And AlphaCode 2 is also here.

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:48.050
The first version was roughly as good as half
the humans in coding, and now, better than

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:51.280
85% of the human competitors.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:54.540
All this in just one version change.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.629
So, what can it do?

00:03:56.629 --> 00:04:02.349
Well, it can break down a written task, and
come up with efficient solutions.

00:04:02.349 --> 00:04:08.730
Here, it came up with a solution using dynamic
programming, this is a college-level computer

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:15.519
science algorithm that breaks down a big,
difficult problem into smaller, easier problems.

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:18.320
Such a short, elegant solution.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:22.019
And make no mistake, this is not just coding.

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:26.110
This is reasoning, understanding, and synthesis.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.110
Loving it.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:33.520
And now, you can have this incredible digital
mind as a companion, or even as a teacher

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.620
in your journeys.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:41.430
And by double-checking and repairing its own
answers, it can now write you a web app in

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.650
less than a minute.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:48.610
It is not going to be perfect, but it is an
incredible first crack at a problem.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:54.260
Once again, ChatGPT can likely do this too
for you at least as well.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:59.720
Now I promised that we will see if it can
do things that ChatGPT cannot.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.690
So, can it?

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:08.850
Well, it is advertised as a universal AI,
let’s talk about that and compare to ChatGPT

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.940
because there are absolutely insane insights
there.

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:18.060
They showcase incredible performance on the
MMLU dataset.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:22.490
When I heard this, my eyes basically popped
out of my head.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.440
So what does this mean?

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:28.310
This is the Massive Multitask Language Understanding
dataset.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:36.260
It contains questions about anatomy, astronomy,
chemistry, formal logic, marketing, management,

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.910
sociology, virology, you name it.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:41.200
So, how good is it?

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:47.830
Well, this is a good human performance, and
this is Gemini.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.100
Yup.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.389
That sort of means superhuman performance.

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:59.410
Now this graph is from the marketing materials,
but we are Fellow Scholars here, we like research

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:02.880
papers better, so there you go.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.130
Ah, much better.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.770
Now let’s look at the comparison.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:13.530
Yes, it claims to beat ChatGPT, but this comparison
has its limits.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:20.039
ChatGPT was benchmarked with 5-shot, which
means that the AI was given 5 somewhat similar

00:06:20.039 --> 00:06:26.110
examples to learn from, where Gemini’s CoT
stands for Chain of Thought.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:28.100
These are important details.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:33.120
This means guiding the AI model through a
step by step reasoning process.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.880
This is not entirely the same process at the
5 shot.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.819
But it gets better!

00:06:39.819 --> 00:06:45.630
Beyond that, in 30 of 32 benchmarks it came
in first.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:51.389
And many of these comparisons are apples to
apples comparisons, you can see the equivalent

00:06:51.389 --> 00:06:55.210
number of shots in the comparisons on many
datasets.

00:06:55.210 --> 00:07:00.879
With this, I think it is fair to conclude
that on these datasets, yes, it can do things

00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:02.430
that ChatGPT cannot.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:07.000
I told you, Google is coming with guns blazing.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:13.699
And wait, if we can have this kind of universality
in an AI… do you remember the example with

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.250
the genome data?

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:16.250
Yes!

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:20.470
This means that it can do this in any area
of science.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.920
Any topic.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.760
Same with the math lessons.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.220
Any lesson works.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:26.640
My goodness!

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:32.389
And Gemini comes in three sizes:
Ultra - this is for the hardest of the hardest

00:07:32.389 --> 00:07:39.199
tasks, pro, this is the bread and butter for
most tasks, and nano, this is a tiny version

00:07:39.199 --> 00:07:42.570
for you to be able to run it in your pocket.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.840
Yes, right on your phone.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:49.229
The Pixel 8 Pro is the first smartphone to
be able to run this.

00:07:49.229 --> 00:07:54.890
Now, good news, I’ll tell you in a moment
how you can try it, but first, two insane

00:07:54.890 --> 00:08:00.000
things from the paper:
One, the training took place across multiple

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.310
data centers.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:07.729
Depending on the methodology, that would possibly
require a computer network that is so fast

00:08:07.729 --> 00:08:10.770
that it basically makes my head fall off.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.830
That is incredible.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.410
Two, look at this.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:22.900
This is something that I could not believe
for years, but it is here, and it is true.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:29.150
Specialist AIs exist, these are techniques
that are incredibly good at one thing, but

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.390
cannot really do anything else.

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:35.849
Like AlphaGo at Go, or AlphaFold at protein
folding.

00:08:35.849 --> 00:08:41.419
And then, there are generalist AIs like GPT-4
and Gemini.

00:08:41.419 --> 00:08:48.940
These can do a lot of things, but not as well
as the specialist AI can do the one thing.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.760
Until now.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:56.360
And this is a historic moment - this is a
universal AI that can beat these specialist

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.870
AIs at their own game.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:05.310
Perhaps because knowing a little less about
your area, but more about the world in general

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:07.700
makes you a better specialist.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.380
That is incredible.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:13.170
A huge philosophical thought that keeps me
up at night.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:14.720
So much to think about!

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:16.910
So, when can we try it?

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.820
Well, according to Google, right about now!

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:25.630
According to them, the pro version is available
right now in Bard.

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:31.839
However, not for me as of the making of this
video, so I am assuming there is a staggered

00:09:31.839 --> 00:09:33.600
rollout of this system.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:37.860
Likely, it will gradually be deployed to all
of us very soon.

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:43.829
I will note that we do not have any business
ties with Google or DeepMind or OpenAI.

00:09:43.829 --> 00:09:48.370
None of our videos were sponsored by them,
including this one of course.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:54.360
According to what we hear from internal documents,
getting this AI and Bard right might be an

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:59.279
existential issue for Google, so they are
putting all their might into it.

00:09:59.279 --> 00:10:01.630
And I have to say it shows.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:02.630
Wow.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:07.750
Very excited to give this a try soon, and
if you see this video, make sure to try Google

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:13.100
Bard, it might already be infused by Gemini
by the time you are watching this.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:15.570
The link is in the video description.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.579
What a time to be alive!

00:10:17.579 --> 00:10:23.019
And if you enjoyed this and if you wish to
see more, become a Fellow Scholar by subscribing

00:10:23.019 --> 00:10:25.029
and hitting the bell icon.

00:10:25.029 --> 00:10:29.209
Checking out our sponsor is also a great way
to support us.

00:10:29.209 --> 00:10:50.089
Thank you so much!

